This product includes software developed by the WEALTH project and its contributors.

WEALTH depends on several open-source libraries. Below is an attribution of major dependencies:

1. NumPy (https://github.com/numpy/numpy)
   License: BSD 3-Clause
   Used for numerical computation and financial modeling.

2. SciPy (https://github.com/scipy/scipy)
   License: BSD 3-Clause
   Used for scientific computation, optimization, and statistical functions.

3. FastMCP (https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol)
   License: MIT License
   Used for Model Context Protocol server interface execution.

4. Pydantic (https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic)
   License: MIT License
   Used for data validation and schema enforcement.

5. yfinance (https://github.com/ranaroussi/yfinance)
   License: Apache License 2.0
   Used for Yahoo Finance market data retrieval.

6. QuantLib (https://github.com/lballabio/QuantLib)
   License: BSD-like (QuantLib License)
   Used for quantitative finance and derivatives pricing.

7. Riskfolio-Lib (https://github.com/dcajasn/Riskfolio-Lib)
   License: BSD 3-Clause
   Used for portfolio optimization and risk modeling.

8. LangGraph (https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph)
   License: MIT License
   Used for agentic workflow orchestration.

9. Polars (https://github.com/pola-rs/polars)
   License: MIT License
   Used for high-performance dataframe operations.

10. DuckDB (https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb)
    License: MIT License
    Used for embedded analytical SQL processing.
